Z||000000||saleenfiero||06-21-2001||01:46 AM||||Okay, first of all I'd like to report another kill on a 75 or so custom F150 truck.  It was done to the nines with what appared to be a 351clev in it.  Killed him, big time.  Anyways, seems when I really romp on the gas in my 86 se auto, past 4000 or 4500, I start to see smoke coming out the back end, looks like oil for the most part.  Doesn't burn any during normal activity, but during races and the like, it seems to....any answers why?  Engines got 74k miles on it||||reg||1
